\f1\b \cf0 10 pairs + 10 trios + 5 quartets + 1 quintet = 26 resonant groupings.
\f2\b0 \
The Sages' pentagram gives those five a deliberately regular geometry. Johnny's phase compensation and control system lets him bring several groupings into stable coherence simultaneously.\
And here is the useful irony:\

\f1\b it works.
\f2\b0 \
It does not explode.\
It produces a cleaner result.\
It gives them 
\f1\b Missing Socks
\f2\b0 .\
That result should appear to disprove Chip.\
Johnny can quite reasonably conclude that Chip's problem was crude three-disc engineering, excessive speed and uncontrolled resonance. Johnny has five discs, better control, a symmetric configuration and lower operating speeds.\
But the reader later discovers that this inference is exactly backwards.\
Chip feared 
\f1\b coherence
\f2\b0 .\
Johnny regards coherence as his success criterion.\
That is a very good trap.\
The \'93Missing Socks\'94 result then becomes more than a plot discovery. It is the reward that teaches Johnny the wrong lesson:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \strokec2 More discs + better coherence = better communication.
\f2\b0 \strokec2 \
So naturally he wants to improve the machine further (and he can\'92t resist the temptation of reintroducing rotation speed. Note that two spinning effects are possible with the new apparatus: \
1) disc harnesses mounted on the elliptical track rotate around the track\
2) each disc harness internally spins its disc on a axis like tossing a coin.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 4. What remains for the final confrontation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f2 This is where 
\f1\b closed resonance
\f2\b0  belongs.\
It should be absent from Hayley's early evidence and absent from the big historical diversion.\
The Rotherhithe investigation contained one deeply technical anomaly that did not matter to Hayley's immediate question and was never reproduced:\
